  "description": "(RT-12 v2) The CircleAI mesh hand-off router. When the local device\n      cannot hold the model a turn needs, the router borrows a stronger\n      peer's brain: it queries the CircleAI.Networking IMeshCapabilityRegistry\n      for peers advertising that model with enough spare KV budget, picks the\n      best one, delegates the completion over any reachable INetworkTransport\n      (hotspot / LAN / Aether mesh), and falls back to a local or smaller\n      model when no peer is available or the peer fails. Also ships a real\n      IMeshCapabilityBroadcaster (AetherMeshCapabilityBroadcaster) that\n      publishes OUR advertisement over the transport, replacing the RT-12 v1\n      no-op. This package CONSUMES a transport; it does not implement one. The\n      zero-infrastructure BLE / Wi-Fi Direct peer discovery that lets phones\n      find each other with no router lives in AetherNet (the aether-protocol\n      repo), not here.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
